@page "/HowItWorks/foreign-currency"
@using InvestmentTaxCalculator.Components

<HowItWorksGuideLayout PageAddress="HowItWorks/foreign-currency">
    <ChildContent>
        <div class="section">
            <p>
                Currency other than pounds is an asset for Capital Gains Tax. When you buy US shares, you first acquire
                dollars and then dispose of them. If the pound value of the dollars changed while you held them, there is a
                gain or loss on the currency as well as on the shares.
            </p>
            <h2 class="section-title">How the app finds currency trades</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Currency trades come from <strong>Interactive Brokers</strong> statements only. Each movement of a
                    non-sterling currency in the statement of funds becomes a trade in that currency. Money coming in is an
                    acquisition and money going out is a disposal. Transfers between IBKR accounts ("System Transfer") are
                    left out.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Each movement is valued in pounds at the IBKR conversion rate for that day.
                </li>
                <li>
                    You can also add currency trades by hand on the <a href="AddTradePage" class="link-styled">Add Manual
                    Entries</a> page, or leave currency out by unticking "Load FX" on the
                    <a href="MainCalculatorPage" class="link-styled">Import data</a> page.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2 class="section-title">How they are calculated</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    Each currency is treated like a share: it has its own Section 104 pool, and the same-day, 30-day and
                    pool rules apply to it.
                </li>
                <li>Currency gains and losses are reported under "Other property, assets and gains".</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="alert alert-info alert-custom" role="note">
                Whether currency held with a broker is chargeable can depend on your circumstances. Check before you
                report these gains, and leave currency out of the import if it does not apply to you.
            </div>
        </div>
    </ChildContent>
    <FurtherReading>
        <li><a href="https://cgtvisualiser.co.uk/guides/foreign-currency-shares/" class="link-styled" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CGT Visualiser: foreign currency shares</a> (independent site)</li>
        <li><a href="HowItWorks/net-proceeds" class="link-styled">Net proceeds and fees</a>: how share trades in other currencies are converted</li>
    </FurtherReading>
</HowItWorksGuideLayout>
